; OHLC bars over a market feed.
;
; Producers publish raw prices on MARKET.<SYM> (e.g. MARKET.AAPL "182.34").
; A bar closes either every 60 ticks per symbol or every wall-clock minute,
; depending on the window descriptor. On close, `bar` emits four sub-subjects:
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.open   first price in the bar
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.high   max price seen
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.low    min price seen
;   MARKET.AAPL.bar.close  last price seen in the bar
;
; State is per (rule, subject, window kind), so each ticker builds its
; own bars and tick + time forms keep distinct slots. The in-progress
; bar is part of the snapshot, so a restart mid-bar resumes without
; losing the open / high / low collected so far. Time bars also close
; from the server's clock walker if a window elapses without a new tick.

; Tick bars: every 60 trades, regardless of how long that takes.
(on "MARKET.*"
  (bar 60 payload-float))

; Wall-clock bars, aligned to whole minutes. Useful when you want a
; clean per-minute chart row regardless of trade rate.
;(on "MARKET.*"
;  (bar :ms 60000 payload-float))

; Downstream alerting can sit on the closed-bar stream and stay clean of
; intra-bar noise. Example: alert if the bar's close jumps by >= 1.0
; from the prior bar's close on the same symbol.
(on "MARKET.*.bar.close"
  (when (>= (abs (delta payload-float)) 1.0)
    (publish (str-concat "alerts.market." (subject-token 1)) payload)))
